Subject: [PATCH] Fix the stuck narrative heading; frame + zoom the hero embed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two fixes, same page:

- 'La sfida' (and any other narrative heading) could outlive its body
  text. Payload only stores null for a richText field never touched;
  once an editor opens it and clears it, what's saved is an empty-but-
  structured document instead, which is truthy. narrative.filter(s =>
  s.body) was gating the heading on that truthiness, so clearing a
  field's text left its heading behind forever. New src/lib/rich-text.ts
  exports hasRichText(), which actually checks for text in the tree,
  and the page now filters with that instead.

- The hero embed now matches what was asked for over the previous
  patch: framed and rounded like the inline embed (LiveEmbedBlock)
  rather than square-cornered full-bleed like heroMedia, and a second,
  continuous animation layered on the existing mask-curtain reveal —
  data-parallax="zoom" (new in scroll-reveal.tsx) scrubs the frame's
  contents from 1.15x down to true size exactly as far as the reader
  has scrolled, rather than firing once like every other reveal. The
  zoom lives on an inner, overflow-hidden element so it never touches
  the frame's own rounded corners.
